THE CODE IS MIT. THE DICTIONARY IS NOT, AND THE DIFFERENCE MATTERS.

This licence covers the software in this repository. It does not and cannot
relicense the language data the software is built on, which arrives under
terms set by the people who made it:

  Estonian forms, paradigms and example sentences
      From Ekilex, the lexicographic database of the Institute of the
      Estonian Language (Eesti Keele Instituut). Licensed CC BY 4.0.
      Attribution required. https://ekilex.ee

  English glosses
      From English Wiktionary, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 by its contributors.
      Attribution required, and share-alike: a work built on this text has
      to be offered on the same terms. https://en.wiktionary.org

  Synthesised speech
      From TartuNLP at the University of Tartu, fetched at runtime and
      cached. Not redistributed as part of this repository.
      https://tartunlp.ai

`prisma/data/expanded.json` is a build product of the first two, so the
share-alike clause reaches it: it may be redistributed, and a redistribution
carries CC BY-SA 4.0 rather than this licence. Nothing about that is a
restriction on the code around it.

Both attributions are rendered in the running app, on the sign-in page, in
the landing page footer and on /terms, which is where a licence of this shape
expects to find them rather than in a file only a developer opens.
